    {
      "id": "2027-Quan-2-4",
      "entry": {
        "title": "2027 Quantitative Methods Mod2-Q4",
        "itemBody": "<p>How does the risk–return trade-off principle affect asset allocation among investors with different objectives?</p>",
        "feedback": {
          "neutral": ""
        },
        "interactionData": {
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "f5a8fa97-55df-4adf-80d1-1e79462ec109",
              "itemBody": "<p>A. It encourages all investors to prioritize high-risk assets for maximum returns.</p>",
              "position": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "cbadfebb-ce05-4cb8-b987-41b60a8287b7",
              "itemBody": "<p>B. It leads investors to allocate assets based on their risk tolerance and return objectives.</p>",
              "position": 2
            },
            {
              "id": "18217c13-9e10-4c80-8767-1e6e02c97acb",
              "itemBody": "<p>C. It suggests that low-risk assets offer the highest potential returns.</p>",
              "position": 3
            }
          ]
        },
